  "about": "Twenty-one solids with the bar and the bulk longitudinal speed in two separate columns, which is the reason this table is worth holding beside the others: most compilations print one speed and leave the reader to guess which. Eleven of the twenty-one print a rule rather than a Poisson ratio and ten print no bar speed, and a rule is served as an absent field rather than shifted out of the way. The table's last column, the product of critical frequency and thickness, is not held: it reproduces the air speed squared over 1.8 times the speed in the row, so it is a quantity this library recomputes rather than a reading it keeps. One modulus is refused as a misprint. The appendix credits several sources at the foot without saying which row came from which, so no row carries an attribution.",
